  "result": "PASS_287_NATIVE_AND_SCOPED_EXACT_JAR_STOCK_CLIENT",
  "scope": "Phase-specific persistent target uncertainty for new automatic item mutations on exact owner/dimension/target routes, preserving existing wireless journal behavior.",
  "contract": {
    "phase_hooks": "Optional ConservingItems.PhasedEscrow hooks select extraction or insertion immediately before the matching block hook and executed foreign mutation. Existing non-phased escrows keep their previous behavior.",
    "contexts": "Automatic extraction reserves the captured source target. Insertion/known-pending flush reserves the captured destination target. A failure retains only its active phase token; a validated earlier phase does not leave the other target fenced.",
    "retry": "Validated healthy phase settlement removes only its own token even if known escrow remains. A well-formed executed refusal can retry its held quantity on a later tick without permanent journal deadlock.",
    "discovery": "Source/destination coordinates are captured before capability discovery; owner and route snapshots are revalidated after discovery before executing a transfer.",
    "idle_allocations": "Automatic token UUIDs are generated lazily when executed mutation phase hooks are reached. No measured performance gain is claimed.",
    "persistence": "Reuse the bounded per-dimension Schema 1 owner/target journal and target reference counts. Capacity/malformed-data guards and opaque preservation remain intact. New cases save/load the actual compressed world-data file in a fresh MapStorage within the same server process; this is not crash/process-restart acceptance."
  },
